Tick tracks task dependencies via `BlockedBy` (stored on task) plus `Parent` for hierarchical relationships. There is no explicit `Blocks` field â€” the reverse relationship is computed via query. All the data exists but there's no way to visualize the dependency graph.

This is purely a presentation concern â€” no data model changes needed. The formatter infrastructure (`Formatter` interface with toon/pretty/JSON implementations) is already in place. The existing `tick dependency add/remove` subcommand pattern means `tick dependency tree` fits naturally.

