### Blocker Type: Dependency Blockers Only

A task can be "blocked" in two senses:
1. **Dependency-blocked**: has unclosed entries in the `dependencies` table
2. **Children-blocked**: has open/in-progress children (parent waiting on child work)

Only **dependency blockers** on ancestors propagate down to affect descendant readiness. The "has open children" state is structural â€” it's the normal state for any parent whose children are the work to be done. A parent with open children isn't externally blocked; it's just waiting for its own subtasks to complete.

If children-blocked propagated, leaf tasks would never be ready since their parent always has open children (the leaf task itself).

### Traversal Depth: Full Ancestor Chain

The ancestor check walks the **full ancestor chain** to the root, not just the immediate parent.

**Why not immediate parent only:** Intermediate grouping tasks create a gap. Example:
```
Phase 1 (open)
Phase 2 (open, blocked_by: Phase 1)
  â””â”€ Group A (open, no own blockers)
      â””â”€ subtask-X (open)
```
With immediate-parent-only, subtask-X checks Group A (not blocked), so subtask-X incorrectly appears ready despite Phase 2 being dependency-blocked.

**Why full chain is safe:** Recursive CTE is an established pattern in the codebase (`queryDescendantIDs()` in `list.go`). Ancestor chains are typically shallow (2-4 levels), so performance is a non-issue.©work_unit¢v1©work_type¤epic¥phase­specification¥topic¶blocked-ancestor-readyªconfidence¤high«source_fileÙ]/Users/leeovery/Code/tick/.workflows/v1/specification/blocked-ancestor-ready/specification.md©timestampÏ␀␀ßİ ,©embeddingÜ␀Ë?š\␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¥Ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¯”␀␀␀␀␀Ë?™¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë?šp␀␀␀␀␀Ë?’ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë?)ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿À␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…␀␀␀␀␀Ë?£␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?´␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿”␀␀␀␀␀Ë?bD␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ŸH␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë?|Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿t␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¡h␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¦␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë?´ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’`␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢X␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿˜È␀␀␀␀␀Ë?qH␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‹@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?}␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢D␀␀␀␀␀Ë?@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‰␀␀␀␀␀Ë?”È␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë?•ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ƒÔ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?h¬␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿•`␀␀␀␀␀Ë?y@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ˆä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?”␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Œl␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ ”␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¬Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?l␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‹␀␀␀␀␀Ë?®@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?†°␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Šü␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜L␀␀␀␀␀Ë?dÜ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?–␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿R¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿wl␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿®ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‰¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿–è␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿=␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿—t␀␀␀␀␀Ë?›@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?x␀␀␀␀␀Ë?†´␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ŠÜ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿uh␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Rì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¦Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿} ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Œô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‰T␀␀␀␀␀Ë?|8␀␀␀␀␀Ë?³␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¬␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿!ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿†Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œ`␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‰ˆ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Mà␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢t␀␀␀␀␀Ë?† ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿qÀ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿§T␀␀␀␀␀Ë?r¸␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿£È␀␀␀␀␀Ë?—t␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿µ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¦H␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿cœ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿d<␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…P␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Ÿ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿– ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿”L␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¦d␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë?t ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¥ˆ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿±␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿šô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿°Ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë?§T␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Š¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿4␀␀␀␀␀Ë?³0␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¨Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¯␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’°␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‚Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢ ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿†¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿°L␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ƒè␀␀␀␀␀Ë?–D␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë? Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?€<␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ˆ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¨Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿qÄ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’|␀␀␀␀␀Ë?–ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?§Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Dt␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë?G”␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‘X␀␀␀␀␀Ë?—\␀␀␀␀␀Ë?pÀ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢Ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿“0␀␀␀␀␀Ë?™ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢p␀␀␀␀␀Ë? \␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Šp␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿~␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿~À␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¥d␀␀␀␀␀Ë?´␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿È␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢(␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‡T␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¡ ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?t␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë?t␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œ´␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Œì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿r”␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿šT␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿yÌ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Ÿ¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜È␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‘Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?SÔ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿„(␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿dä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‘t␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ª ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…è␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿“4␀␀␀␀␀Ë?§␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿œ|␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿³ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ƒx␀␀