␀␀Ë?ˆ`␀␀␀␀␀Ë?†X␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?°<␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‰ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?”␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?—4␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ƒà␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿jÀ␀␀␀␀␀£275Š¢idÙGready-includes-in-progress-specification-ready-includes-in-progress-008§contentÚë## Acceptance Criteria

1. An unblocked `in_progress` leaf task appears in `tick ready`.
2. An unblocked `open` leaf task still appears in `tick ready` (no regression).
3. A `blocked` `in_progress` task (unclosed blocker, or blocked ancestor) appears in `tick blocked` and **never** in `tick ready`.
4. Every live task (`open` or `in_progress`) appears in exactly one of `tick ready` / `tick blocked`; `done`/`cancelled` appear in neither.
5. In `tick ready` (and `tick list --ready`), `in_progress` tasks sort above all `open` tasks; within each band, `priority ASC, created ASC` holds.
6. `tick list` and `tick list --blocked` retain the existing `priority ASC, created ASC` ordering, unchanged.
7. `tick ready --count 1` returns the top unblocked in-flight task when one exists, otherwise the top unblocked open task.
8. `tick ready --status open` returns unstarted ready work; `tick ready --status in_progress` returns resumptions only; `--status done`/`--status cancelled` return empty.
9. `tick stats` blocked count equals `(Open + InProgress) âˆ’ Ready` and is never negative; the ready count includes unblocked `in_progress` tasks.
10. An `in_progress` parent that exists only via the start-cascade does not appear in `tick ready`; only its leaf does.©work_unitºready-includes-in-progress©work_type§feature¥phase­specification¥topicºready-includes-in-progressªconfidence¤high«source_fileÙ_.workflows/ready-includes-in-progress/specification/ready-includes-in-progress/specification.md©timestampÏ␀␀|ÎÄ©embeddingÜ␀Ë?␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ª␀␀␀␀␀Ë?zä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?è␀␀␀␀␀Ë?|¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿8␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‘Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë?› ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?«à␀␀␀␀␀Ë?$␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿›␀␀␀␀␀Ë?r¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¦ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë?šÜ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿›␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë?8␀␀␀␀␀Ë?§œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?­è␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢À␀␀␀␀␀Ë?zÜ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¸␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿š„␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‘<␀␀␀␀␀Ë?…␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë?w¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë?šØ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‰Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?vl␀␀␀␀␀Ë?’h␀␀␀␀␀Ë?…H␀␀␀␀␀Ë?’,␀␀␀␀␀Ë?©œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿v˜␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Ÿ(␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿–Ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢x␀␀␀␀␀Ë?fŒ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿z¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ˆ¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‘␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿©°␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œl␀␀␀␀␀Ë?€␀␀␀␀␀Ë?–␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿}\␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿uÜ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿^p␀␀␀␀␀Ë?L␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‘À␀␀␀␀␀Ë?©4␀␀␀␀␀Ë?’@␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿˜p␀␀␀␀␀Ë? ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿zD␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‘␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿˜À␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Ÿ4␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‘l␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ª4␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿˜À␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¤ ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¡ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿’␀␀␀␀␀Ë?±L␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿vÌ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜˜␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿dÄ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?|L␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?%<␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿z\␀␀␀␀␀Ë?`␀␀␀␀␀Ë?UØ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‹<␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¯ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë?›Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ƒ”␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‡␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¡Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¢è␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¥␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ŠØ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‡8␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿`D␀␀␀␀␀Ë?rL␀␀␀␀␀Ë? p␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¡Ğ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¢␀␀␀␀␀Ë? Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿®4␀␀␀␀␀Ë?„è␀␀␀␀␀Ë?±¤␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿®Œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿®¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¬Ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë?œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿–`␀␀␀␀␀Ë?P␀␀␀␀␀Ë?—d␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿—¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¯4␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‡@␀␀␀␀␀Ë?˜´␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿wD␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¯\␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿©Ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿™L␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿™È␀␀␀␀␀Ë?ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‚H␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿Š|␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿´Ü␀␀␀␀␀Ë?X°␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿h␀␀␀␀␀Ë?— ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¨˜␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë?c€␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿(␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿oP␀␀␀␀␀Ë?£,␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¡x␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿è␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤h␀␀␀␀␀Ë?n␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ƒì␀␀␀␀␀Ë?–$␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ l␀␀␀␀␀Ë?€Ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿† ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¸␀␀␀␀␀Ë?À␀␀␀␀␀Ë?È␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿–\␀␀␀␀␀Ë?_␀␀␀␀␀Ë?u␀␀␀␀␀Ë?”␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë?~␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‡<␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¤¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿š€␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿…¼␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿œœ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤¸␀␀␀␀␀Ë?dÈ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?š␀␀␀␀␀Ë?†œ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¤Ä␀␀␀␀␀Ë?{¨␀␀␀␀␀Ë?‚L␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿0␀␀␀␀␀Ë?Ì␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿a4␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿oÄ␀␀␀␀␀Ë?“ô␀␀␀␀␀Ë?X␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿© ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿z$␀␀␀␀␀Ë?°´␀␀␀␀␀Ë?„ˆ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿­à␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¨Ø␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿cÄ␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿‹d␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿–␀␀␀␀␀Ë?¯l␀␀␀␀␀Ë?st␀␀␀␀␀Ë¿¬Ô␀